1;6.^IAll setting out dimensions and levels shall be as per Architectural drawing. \P{\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;7.^IFor the detailed general notes and typical reinforcement details}  {\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;refer } {\fTimes New Roman|b
  3
0|i0|c238|p18;Drg.No.DRIQ/BL/} {\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;/}2012 \P\pi0,l0,t557.46981,836.20472;^Isheet No.1/3,2/3,3/3.\P\pi-557.46981,l557.46981,t557.46981;8.^IThe structure is designed for seismic zone III as per IS 1893 Part I-2016           
  3
    \P{\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;9.^IWall loads are taken only for the beams wherever walls are shown in the A}r{\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;chitectural} {\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;drawing.}\P{\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c238|p18;10.^IDo
  3
 not scale of the drawing, only figured dimensions shall be follo}wed. \P{\A0;11.^IMain slab projections, sunshades, vertical board works, jally works & lintels are to be provided as per Architectural requirements.\P12.^IPoly carbonate sheet and suppor
  3
ting structures should be as per fabricator's details and shall be provided where ever specified in Architectural drawing.\P13.^IThe structure is designed for (2B + G+3) floors to (G+3) floors only according to the Ground slope as per Architectural dr
  3
awing. No future expansion for any upper floors is considered in the design.\P14.^IThe slope to drain off rain water from roof terrace and all other roofs shall be provided in the slab/ beam form work itself, without affecting the Architectural elevat
  1
ion requirements of the building.}
