\pxl1,t4;    SPECIAL NOTE:- {\A1;\C256;\P\pl0,tz;\P\pi-3,l6.32228,t6.32228;}1.^ID{\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c186|p18;esign of foundation is based on the soil investigation report }and additional recommendation for foundation {\fTimes New Roman|b0|i0|c18
  1
6|p18;prepared } by {\C1;M/s. ULCCS Ltd.} and forwarded by the Executive  Engineer, Buildings  Division, {\C1;Thalassery} as per letter  {\C1;D6/PWD/BLDB/201/2020 dt.13.12.2021}. Based on the above report, open foundations are adopted with an SBC of 
  1
{\C1;280kN/m²} at a founding depths varies from 1.5m to 2.5m. \P2.^IAs the foundations are laid at different levels and heavy soil excavation is needed in the construction stage, proper safety measures shall be taken to avoid soil slippage. Expert Geo
  1
technical advice may be sought for proper shuttering methods. \P3.^IThe soil at founding level shall be fully compacted soil Layer/Rock formation to achieve the specified value of safe bearing capacity. \P4.^IThe feasibility of the proposed foundation 
  1
size and depth shall be studied while setting out the proposed building in order to avoid any clash/disturbance to the existing foundations/structures.
